// TEST: entry=29 shape=reference status=run subject=examples/arca/arca.exsc host=examples/arca/proba.c header=examples/arca/arca.h driver=examples/arca/proba.py reference=tar seed=1 min-cases=3000 min-admitted=300 min-refused=300 mutants=entry29/mutantes.tsv

// §14 entry 29 -- the tar-header judge `examples/arca/arca.exsc`, held to
// GNU tar: every archive the judge ADMITS, GNU tar reads as exactly the
// members the judge listed, each a regular file or a directory, with exit
// status 0. The first entry of §14's SIXTH shape, differential agreement with
// a reference implementation (§14, "The sixth shape").
//
// THIS FILE CARRIES NO PROGRAM, and that is the design, not an omission. The
// subject is examples/arca/arca.exsc, named by `subject=` and compiled from
// where it lives: a copy here would be a second program that can drift from
// the one reliquary links, and a differential over the copy would prove
// nothing about the original. (The same reason entry 26's fixture says where
// its legs are carried.) A comment-only module is valid and checks clean.
// The rest of the entry is in four places:
//
//   examples/arca/proba.c    the host loop reliquary runs in Rust, in C
//   examples/arca/arca.h     its C face, force-included so a drifted
//                            signature is a build error
//   examples/arca/proba.py   the generator (seeded), the comparison with
//                            GNU tar, and the corpus checks around it
//   entry29/mutantes.tsv     wrong variants of arca that the differential,
//                            by itself, must catch
//
// WHAT THE RUNNER (tests/run.sh, reference_entry) REQUIRES, and what each
// requirement is for:
//
//   seed=1               recorded in every result line. The driver mutates a
//                        real GNU-tar archive of reliquary's own pack flags,
//                        3000 times, with random.Random(seed).
//   disagreements == 0   one-directional: the judge may REFUSE what tar
//                        would read -- most mutants are refused -- and the
//                        entry says so by counting them, never by calling
//                        them agreement. It may never ADMIT what tar reads
//                        differently, or reads with a failing exit status.
//   min-cases=3000       the driver's whole fuzz, not a prefix of it.
//   min-admitted=300     measured 807 admitted at seed 1 (README: 4,629 over
//   min-refused=300      seeds 1-6, 18,000 mutants). A run that admitted
//                        nothing, or refused nothing, compared nothing; the
//                        floors sit well under the measurement so a different
//                        GNU tar moves the count without failing the entry,
//                        and well over 0 so a gate that stopped admitting
//                        (or stopped refusing) fails it.
//   four builds          gcc and clang at -O0 and -O2, UBSan, and the four
//                        must report identical counts.
//   mutants              each must produce disagreements > 0 in the same
//                        driver: three wrong arcas (types unchecked, numeric
//                        fields unchecked, checksum unchecked). The other
//                        three mutants examples/arca/proba_c.sh uses are
//                        caught by the driver's hostile CORPUS, not by the
//                        differential, so they are left to that script: they
//                        show the driver can fail, not that THIS shape can.
//
// WHAT PASSING DOES NOT PROVE. 3000 seeded mutants of one archive's headers
// are a sample of the input space, not the space: the mutator flips one to
// three bytes, favouring a handful of header offsets, and never produces a
// header from nothing. Agreement with GNU tar 1.35 says nothing about
// bsdtar, busybox tar, or a different GNU tar. The reference itself builds
// the base archive, so exact counts move with its version (the floors are
// the contract, not the counts). Zero disagreements is "none found", and the
// two findings in examples/arca/README.md are evidence that the method
// finds things, not that it has found everything.
//
// When GNU tar or python3 is absent the entry is DEFERRED, naming which, and
// is not counted as passing.
